Subject: [#94-7-249] us.* Hierarchy CFV

In <9407290158.AA22246@geech.gnu.ai.mit.edu>, Shawn O'Connor writes:
> Since the argument against the us.* hierarchy has just been posted 
> here, I'm forwarding an argument in favor of us.* that appeared on 
> cypherpunks.  Any other arguments for or against?

Yes, against, because it should be difficult to create a newsgroup,
because the namespace (the highest level index, so to speak) is
already complex enough and its growth should be restrained until a
more intelligent indexing method is available.

Right now we have:

newsgroup namespace tree
	subject:'s
		threads
	keywords
		text

and we depend on the top part of this hierarchy too much. Time to
get on with better ways of specifying the content we want  to see.

